        {
          "type": "Claim",
          "identifier": "protocerebral-bridge-layered-transmitter-architecture",
          "role": "empirical",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": "The protocerebral bridge (PCB) of Uloborus diversus displays a layered neurotransmitter architecture: GABAergic (anti-GAD) immunoreactivity defines a nearly complete swath of the neuropil; TDC2 (octopaminergic/tyraminergic) fills heavy chains of puncta along the posterior edge; proctolin forms a tight thin band primarily at the medial end; and ChAT (cholinergic) immunoreactivity forms a distinct thin layer on both the anterior and posterior edges, most clearly on the lateral portion."
            }
          ],
          "epistemicStrength": "strong",
          "relations": [
